-- title:
--   Com Main Of Commutativity Points
-- statement:
--   **Full-slice commutativity from point-measurement commutativity.**
--
--   Let $S$ be a symmetric strategy with normalized state $\psi$, and let $G^x$ be an indexed family of degree-$d$ polynomial projective measurements. Assume the point-measurement products satisfy the state-dependent squared operator-distance relation with error `commutativityPointsError` at $\gamma$, sampled uniformly over pairs of points in $\mathbb{F}_q^{m+1}$. Also assume $\gamma\ge0$, point consistency and strong self-consistency at error $\zeta$, and the positive-witness residual and domination conditions in `SliceBoundednessInput`. Then, for the uniform distribution $\mathcal U$ on full-slice questions, the ordered and reversed full-slice product families satisfy
--
--   $$
--   \operatorname{SDDOpRel}_{\psi,\mathcal U}\left(P_L,P_R;30m\left(\gamma^{1/4}+\zeta^{1/4}+\left(\frac{d}{q}\right)^{1/4}\right)\right).
--   $$
--
--   Here $P_L$ and $P_R$ are the ordered and reversed products of the two slice measurements. This theorem applies the evaluated-to-full transport lemma after deriving its evaluated-side hypothesis from point-measurement commutativity.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Commutativity.comMain_of_commutativityPoints`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
